Good Morning,

 

MOMENT OF SILENCE:  We pause this morning for a moment of silence to honor
the memory of Charlene Fisher, wife of our dear Joke List friend and
frequent contributor Bill Fisher:

 

I'm grieved to tell you that after courageously fighting Cancer for over a
year, my wonderful wife of nearly 53 years Charlene passed away last night
Feb 12. She was an incredible woman and will be dearly missed. 

 

We know that God is with her and our family. She is in a better place
because of her faith. I am looking forward to meeting her in heaven someday.


 

Thank you all for your continued prayers.

 

Charlene, you have Gone West.  Not alone into the sunset, but into the
company of friends who have gone before you.  Rest in peace.

 

On that somber note, we none the less celebrate Valentine's Day today.
Please give your Sweetheart a special hug in memory of Charlene.

 

Our jokes today come from our friends at Jokes 2 U.

 

****************************************************************************
*** 

 

Jim asked his friend, Tony, whether he had bought his wife anything for
Valentine's Day. 

 

'Yes,' came the answer from Tony who was a bit of a chauvinist, 'I've bought
her a belt and a bag.'

 

'That was very kind of you,' Jim added, 'I hope she appreciated the
thought.' 

 

Tony smiled as he replied, 'So do I, and hopefully the vacuum cleaner will
work better now.'

 

 

Jeremy visited a florist's shop which showed a large sign that read, 'Say It
With Flowers.' 

 

"Wrap up one rose, please" Jeremy demanded of the florist's assistant. 

 

"Only one?", she enquired frowning. 

 

"Ah yes just the one", Jeremy replied. "I'm a man of very few words."' 

 

Steve Sanderson

